  m_Name: PokedexBeardedDragon
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  entryId: bearded_dragon
  commonName: Central Bearded Dragon
  scientificName: Pogona vitticeps
  icon: {fileID: 10904, guid: 0000000000000000f000000000000000, type: 0}
  category: Reptile
  habitat: Arid Deserts & Woodlands
  height: 0.45 - 0.60 m
  weight: 0.25 - 0.50 kg
  diet: Omnivore
  rarity: Common
  shortDescription: A stout, desert-dwelling lizard equipped with specialized spiky
    scales and an expandable pouch under its throat.
  behaviorNotes: Mainly active during the day. They love basking on hot desert rocks
    to regulate their temperature and communicate using rhythmic head bobs and arm
    waves.
  observationTips: Look closely at elevated perches like sunlit boulders or low-hanging
    branches where they sit completely still to survey the environment.
  funFact: When threatened or defending territory, they puff out their throat pouch,
    which turns a dramatic jet-black color, making them look like they have a dark
    beard.
  facts:
  - They are native to the warm, semi-arid interior deserts and shrublands of Australia.
  - To show submission or de-escalate tension with another lizard, they will lift
    a front leg and rotate it in a slow, circular 'waving' motion.
  - While they are excellent climbers, they spend cold desert nights burrowed under
    sand or hidden away inside deep rock crevices to escape frost.
